# Git workflow

Integration branch is `dev`. Release branch is `master`.

- Start from an up-to-date `dev`.
- Put new work on `feature/<short-name>`.
- Put fixes on `bugfix/<short-name>`.
- Do not commit feature or bugfix work directly on `dev` or `master`.
- Merge a finished feature or bugfix branch into `dev`.
- Put a commit on `master` only for a real release, and tag that commit (`vMAJOR.MINOR.PATCH`).
- Do not leave unreleased development commits on `master`.

Release path: `feature/*` or `bugfix/*` → `dev` → when the user calls a real release, merge `dev` into `master` and tag that commit.

Create a commit, merge, tag, or push only when the user asks. Do not force-push, skip hooks, or rewrite published history unless the user explicitly asks.
